body:json {
  {
    "content": "title: ExpressJS Ace: Master the Web with This Quiz!\ndescription: Unlock the power of ExpressJS and become a web development pro! This interactive quiz app is your ultimate guide to mastering the fundamentals of the ExpressJS framework. Dive into a series of carefully crafted quizzes covering routing, middleware, templating, and more. Track your progress, compare scores with friends, and receive detailed explanations for every question. Whether you're a beginner taking your first steps or a seasoned developer brushing up your skills, ExpressJS Ace will sharpen your knowledge and boost your confidence. Get ready to build blazing-fast, efficient, and modern web applications – Download now and begin your ExpressJS journey!\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: Which HTTP method is typically used to retrieve data from a server?\noptions:\n1. POST\n2. PUT\n3. GET [correct]\n4. DELETE\ntags: Expressjs, HTTP, Routing\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: Middleware functions in ExpressJS have access to the request object, the response object, and the next middleware function in the stack.\ncorrect: true\ntags: Expressjs, Middleware\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Explain the purpose of the `next()` function in ExpressJS middleware.\ntags: Expressjs, Middleware\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following are common templating engines used with ExpressJS?\noptions:\n1. Pug (formerly Jade) [correct]\n2. EJS [correct]\n3. Handlebars\n4. ASP.NET\ntags: Expressjs, Templating\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What is the primary purpose of `express.json()` middleware?\noptions:\n1. To serve static files.\n2. To parse JSON request bodies. [correct]\n3. To handle routing.\n4. To create sessions.\ntags: Expressjs, Middleware\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: ExpressJS can only be used to build web applications that serve HTML.\ncorrect: false\ntags: Expressjs, Web Applications\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Describe how you would define a route in ExpressJS to handle a GET request to the path `/users`.\ntags: Expressjs, Routing\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: What are the benefits of using ExpressJS?\noptions:\n1. Simplifies routing and middleware setup. [correct]\n2. Provides a robust set of features for building web applications. [correct]\n3. Offers a steep learning curve.\n4. Automatically manages database connections.\ntags: Expressjs, Web Development\n"
  }
}
